00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
now that we've had our hands on apple's  m1 macbook air and macbook pro for over  two months  i figured i'd revisit the topic of which  one of these m1 max you should buy  except this time there's a twist  what if you should actually hold off and  wait for the future  redesigned apple silicon macbooks  instead because yes  we are expecting some new fully  redesigned models in the near future  and i'm going to be talking about all of  those leaks and rumors  and what to expect from them and believe  it or not some people will  actually be much better off buying an m1  mac  right now instead of waiting but before  i get into  all of that i want to talk about the  differences between the  air and the pro after two full months  first  let me quickly cover the main hardware  differences that  actually matter the macbook air is  completely fanless  while the pro does have one fan the pro  comes with an 8 core gpu at the base  price instead of 7 with the air the pro  also gets a larger 58.2 watt hour  battery  compared to 49.9 on the air and  finally the macbook air starts at 999  compared to 12.99 for the pro those are  the major hardware differences between  the two  so at first glance it seems like the air  is a much  better value and after two months i've  gotta admit that it definitely  is but there are some reasons that  people should be buying the macbook pro  instead and i'll explain in just a  second on the exterior the main  difference is the shape  with the air being more of a wedge shape  instead of a flat slate  shape on the pro because of that  difference the air is a bit more  comfortable for typing  since your palm doesn't dig into the  edge of the macbook  like on the pro by far the biggest  difference is the fact that the air gets  the traditional  function keys while the pro gets the  touch bar  that many people don't like now i  personally prefer  the function keys because i never really  got much use out of the touch bar  in most apps it's easier and faster to  just  use keyboard shortcuts and for adjusting  brightness and audio settings  the function keys are hands down the  better option  what makes this even more interesting  are some very recent leaks and rumors  that point to apple finally ditching the  touch bar  and going back to function keys on the  future macbook pros  and i'm gonna get into the rest of those  interesting leaks in just a minute now  getting back to the air versus pro  the other major difference is the  battery life even though the physical  battery itself  is only around 16 larger on the macbook  pro  somehow the battery life is much much  better  linus tech tips tested the video  playback and they found that the pro's  battery lasted  over 20 hours which is incredible  and it lasted about 7 hours longer than  the macbook air  that's over 50 percent better battery  life with a battery that's only  16 larger and i'd say that this  is by far the biggest factor when you're  trying to decide between these two  now i'm not trying to say that the  battery life on the macbook air is bad  it's better than basically every windows  laptop ever  but the pro is just on a whole nother  level so if battery life is  incredibly important to you then paying  an extra three hundred dollars  is definitely worth it but if you don't  really go out much  and you don't mind plugging it in a  little bit more often  then the air is definitely fine now in  terms of performance  the air is more than enough for most  people even those who need it for  productivity work  like general photo and video editing in  our testing the air held up  extremely well in terms of everything  from logic pro  music production xcode programming  final cut video editing and lightroom  classic  photo editing and those are all tasks  that the intel macbook airs  have never been good at now because of  the m1 chip  you can finally do those tasks with  excellent performance  but the main advantage is that it's  completely  fanless so you never have to worry about  the fan kicking on  ever again with the previous macbook air  the fan would turn on  at the weirdest times like when simply  browsing the web  or even worse while on a zoom call or  watching a movie  which can get extremely annoying since  you can't hear it that well  with the m1 no fan means absolutely  zero noise and even while doing high  performance work  it doesn't get nearly as hot as the  previous intel macbooks would get  no fans also means no dust clogging the  internals of your macbook  which leads to blocked airflow and  overheating  after just a couple of years of use now  because of all of that  it might seem like the added fan on the  pro model  isn't so great after all but after two  months of use  we've noticed that we barely even hear  the fan on the pro  at all we use the fan and temp tracking  app  named tg pro and while doing basic tasks  like web browsing  watching videos or other things like  that the fan on the pro  is almost always completely turned off  not running at all and when doing light  productivity work  the fan turns on but it stays at around  idle speed  and at those speeds you can't hear it  unless you literally put your ear to the  back of the macbook pro  and that's just incredible so because of  that we decided to run  the most intensive heavy workloads on  both of these macbooks  to see if the fan actually made a real  world difference  we exported 500 raw 42 megapixel photos  in lightroom classic  which is just about the heaviest  workload you can put on the cpu and the  ram  and we were honestly expecting a much  bigger difference  the pro was only three and a half  minutes faster  than the fanless air we then switched  over to the graphics side and exported  an 8k  red rock clip in final cut pro which  basically maxes out the graphics  and uses a ton of cpu power and the pro  was only two and a half minutes faster  so to be completely honest  that big of a difference is not worth  the extra 300  for the pro especially since the air  doesn't even have a fan  we then tested out gaming and here there  was actually a difference  with the pro getting around 11 higher  frames per second  but that's only because the pro comes  with an 8 core gpu  compared to 7 on the air we later tested  the top 10 most popular games on twitch  with the m1 macbook pro and we noticed  that after most of the games  the fan speed was barely above idle  which was really impressive considering  that most other laptops  get very loud while gaming but i've  gotta say that if you're crazy about  gaming the future m1x macbooks  are going to be much better as we're  expecting a 16 core gpu  which is going to handle many games  extremely well so if you're all about  gaming  you might want to wait and hold off for  just a little bit longer but getting  back to the air versus pro  i've got to say that if you're trying to  get the best performance  for the buck you should probably just  get the air  and save that 300 and if you really want  to upgrade something  i'd either upgrade the storage or go for  16 gigs of ram  which can help for photo editing and  heavy multitasking  so if i had to close the m1 macbook air  versus pro topic i'd honestly have to  say that  almost everybody should just buy the air  for the better value and this finally  brings us to some more leaks  to solidify our conclusion on not going  for the m1 macbook pro just a few days  ago  both mingxiko and mark german released  reports claiming that  two redesigned macbook pro models are  coming later this year  with quo pointing to a summer release  date now i personally think it makes  sense for apple to announce these  at this year's wwdc conference since  that's when they initially announced  the apple silicon transition last year  but i guess we're just gonna have to  wait and see  in terms of the redesign changes quo is  expecting both 14  and 16-inch macbook pro models with mini  led displays  a new flat edge design like we currently  have on the iphone 12 and the ipad pro  the return of the magsafe charging  connector  more types of ports and of course the  removal of  the touch bar so if you're looking at  the current 13-inch macbook pro  you should definitely consider waiting  just a few more months for these new  models  because apple is likely going to stick  with this new redesign  for many years and these new pros  will also come with a more powerful m1x  chip however i'm almost 100 sure  that the 14 inch macbook pro is gonna  start at either eighteen hundred  or two thousand dollars so if there's no  way you're willing to pay  that much for a laptop then you should  not  wait for them and you might as well just  get an m1 model right now  now on top of those leaks for the pro  models we also have multiple sources  confirming that the next macbook air is  only going to come out in 2022  and if apple releases it in the fall  like they did with the m1 model  that basically means that there won't be  an updated macbook air  for almost two more years and it's  rumored to get the new mini led display  the full redesign and it's likely to  come with a new three nanometer chip  but to be honest it doesn't make sense  to wait that long  before buying a new macbook especially  if you're interested right now  so here's the final rundown if the m1  max  perform well enough for your needs and  you don't want to wait a few months  to spend at least eighteen hundred  dollars on  a new 14-inch macbook pro then we think  that based on all of our testing  most people should probably just buy the  m1  macbook air for 999 dollars  right now especially since the  redesigned model  is not coming until 2022. so hopefully  this video helped you make a decision  and if it did you can find the best  deals on these macbooks down in the  description below  and if you enjoyed this video go ahead  and click the circle above to subscribe  and definitely check out one of those  two videos right over there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video  [Music]

